# `.pubignore` **replaces** `.gitignore` rather than adding to it. Anything not
# listed here goes into the published archive whether git ignores it or not —
# when this file was first created, a 45MB cache under `build/` really did end
# up in the archive.
#
# So everything `.gitignore` blocked that **can actually appear** is carried
# over. `pubspec.lock` and `.DS_Store` are left out because pub excludes them
# itself.

# Build output and tool caches
build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# The example's platform scaffolding. pub.dev's example tab reads
# `example/lib/main.dart` and `example/README.md` — the macOS and web folders
# only grow the archive twentyfold and hold nothing for consumers to read. They
# stay in the repository (the example must be runnable).
example/macos/
example/web/
example/build/
example/.dart_tool/

# What the gates and doc generation produce. One `flutter test --coverage` or
# `dart doc` creates them, and then they ship in the package.
coverage/
**/doc/api/
*.log

# IDE and editor files
.idea/
.atom/
.history
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
*.swp
.metadata

# The reference snapshot. It is not part of the package but the original the
# implementation checked its own output against — see reference/README.md.
reference/

# Repository housekeeping docs. Consumers have no reason to receive them.
# Excluding `docs/` has one more reason — pub warns to rename a top-level `docs`
# to `doc`, but `docs/adr` is the path CLAUDE.md's convention points to, so it
# cannot be renamed. Excluding it keeps the convention and silences the warning.
docs/
CLAUDE.md
GLOSSARY.md
